ot split by row (the seven txs share one return): after Unizen's on-chain message (2024-03-10 09:59:35Z) Yoink sent 'Returning 90% of profits' at 20:38:59Z, but that 0.29808 ETH tx 0xd06abff5 REVERTED (status 0, gas limit 41,511; the recipient is a contract); the resend 0x4f647c4d (block 19407140, 20:40:11Z) succeeded. The vault 0xc70f00cd then sent 12,209.116660 USDT (0xb3482ffe, 20:41:59Z) and 4,327.967358 USDC (0xdac41e41, 20:43:23Z). That is 90.0% of the 7-tx net in each asset (ETH net 0.331214, USDT 13565.685174, USDC 4808.852620); about $17,704 of $19,671. Yoink refused more (message 0x4840a6a4: 'claw that back from the validators'); the bribe claim is supported for block 19393223 (proposer received 2.4507 ETH) but 3.80 ETH of coinbase payments across the seven blocks came back as builder refunds.","returned_pct":null},"incident_raw":{},"timeline_notes":[],"sources":["https://alpha.rekt.news/unizen-rekt (raw/web-unizen/rekt_unizen.html)","https://www.halborn.com/blog/post/explained-the-unizen-hack-march-2024 (raw/web-unizen/halborn_unizen.html)"],"dataset_money":{"scope":"bot-tx","coinbase_eth":3.45211,"paid_to_builder_eth":3.45211,"builder_refund_eth":0.99992,"note":"ETH side only: the bot paid a flat 3.4521105 ETH (msg.value 34,521,105 x 1e11) from its own float, got 0.999920 back from the builder (block's 10-tx 'I can haz block?', index 8) and gas 0.017541; the proposer received 2.450663 ETH. The gain is the 13,565.69 USDT kept, not in bot_net_eth. Net in USD terms: 13,566 - 9,668 = 3,898."},"title":"Unizen: pending USDT","sub_label":"pending USDT","evidence_strength":"medium","evidence_strength_basis":"pending tx measured and victim wallets match, but Yoink's calls are an adaptation of two of five calls, not a byte copy","public_ordering":null,"comparison_policy":null,"caveat":null,"headline":true,"timeline_publication_gaps":[{"tx":"0xc12a4155c2c90707138e4aef8883c8f724371145823e2f661f19b93e5b3a9d6e","kind":"tx","unsupported_fields":["amount 2,176,228.71 US